# eval: raw CVs (PII — derived, anonymized profiles are committed; the source CVs are not) and any
# working *.json dump under data/. The committed datasets are *.jsonl; candidates-export.json and
# any custom --out target are *.json working artifacts, never committed. Pool snapshots
# (data/pools/) are regeneration intermediates — only the frozen dataset.jsonl they feed is
# committed (data/profiles/ label files ARE committed). Fixture reports are
# smoke-test output, not baselines. Extraction-eval reports (Phase F4) have no diff-vs-baseline
# mechanism, so they are run artifacts (the stub one is explicitly "not a quality signal"), never committed.
packages/eval/data/cvs/
packages/eval/data/*.json
packages/eval/data/pools/
packages/eval/reports/*.fixture.json
packages/eval/reports/extraction-*.json

# generated render preview (pnpm email:preview output — a working artifact, never committed)
packages/email/email-preview.html

